+`block_lazy_kdtree_backed<V, Columns=2, Simd=true, Cascade=true>` is an optional
+leaf filter on the same lazy KD engine. Named unary controls are
+`block_lazy_kdtree_1_scalar`, `_1_simd`, `_2_scalar`, and `_2_simd`. They retain
+the same geometry, labels and candidate order. The original lazy backend has
+zero columns. Signed integral coordinates up to 64 bits cache coordinates 1 and
+(for two-column mode) dimension/2, deduplicating dimensions 2/3. Dimension 1 has
+no useful extra coordinate. Floating and unsupported coordinates use the ordinary
+path without column allocation or a column-vector header. The ordinary zero-column
+backend likewise has no filter-vector header. Integral dimension-1 filtered
+variants retain an empty vector header and query wrapper; they are not byte-identical
+to the plain backend. No raw Vector storage or wrapper layout is assumed.
+
+The column labels are immutable in leaf-ID order until staged rebuild publication.
+Retirement never reads a dead payload; a filter survivor must still pass the live
+predicate before its full partial-order comparison. Strictness comes only from
+that full comparison. SIMD compares different points, with at most 16 selected
+lanes. It loads only complete valid stored-leaf chunks, clips candidate enumeration
+to the exact coordinate-0 bound, and uses a scalar tail. There is no padding read,
+query heap scratch or unused floating-point column buffer. Scalar controls use
+the same columns and may still be compiler auto-vectorized.
+
+Storage reports actual retained filter bytes, effective columns and selected
+filter lanes. Existing opt-in query statistics count loaded SIMD chunks and their
+active lanes, scalar active lanes, pre-liveness filter survivors and empty active
+masks. SIMD survivor counts include computed active lanes after an early exact
+witness and may include retired IDs; they are not payload accesses or confirmed
+dominance matches. `comparisons` counts actual live full-order attempts. All filter
+counters are compiled out with the existing statistics gate disabled. These are
+experimental controls; no speedup or default switch is implied.
+
 Define `POSETS_LAZY_KDTREE_STATS=1` consistently across translation units to
 collect query/node/leaf visits, full comparisons, binary searches and bridge
 corrections. Index query counts exclude requests answered by the pending
